From b6e4ebe62ed3370da07f6fe93c2e1e1aad53754f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:02:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] WIP: Quick Share announces under a .local. host name;
 mdns-sd vendored and wired in

rqs_lib 0019 gives the service a valid host name and registers it in
MDnsServer::new, so a refusal reaches the caller; 0020 switches rqs_lib
to the vendored mdns-sd, filters both daemons' sources by the reach
policy and makes the discovery cache fair per source. mdns-sd's patch 2
now forgets a replaced instance's records at once, sweeps when short of
room, and stops the resolve retries of instances that are gone: a flood
test caught orphans of churned instances filling the cache. rqs_lib
tests: a real registration resolved by a second daemon, the responder's
S7 filter and reply limit, and a flood that neither grows the daemon nor
keeps an honest phone off the list. ci/rqs-lib-tests.sh copies the
vendored mdns-sd beside rqs_lib (CONTRACT).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ENZSCiAud5Vs29ugEacpyR
